{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":3328227,"num_turns":126,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"12bb7159-3236-4ecd-a592-3d03b0ce2dfb","total_cost_usd":23.4387435,"usage":{"input_tokens":252,"cache_creation_input_tokens":436853,"cache_read_input_tokens":20365652,"output_tokens":177923,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":80303},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":436853},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"global.anthropic.claude-opus-5[1m]":{"inputTokens":408,"outputTokens":280396,"cacheReadInputTokens":25827036,"cacheCreationInputTokens":942303,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":25.81485175,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"bedrock"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"not_first_party","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The translation is complete and verified. Final state:\n\n## Deliverables\n- **`Cargo.toml`** — `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`, name `translated_rust` (produces `libtranslated_rust.so`, same as the CMake build)\n- **`src/lib.rs`** — 1060 lines, full translation of `c_src/src/lib.c` (758 lines). `cargo build --release` compiles with zero warnings.\n\n## Complete ABI surface — `nm -D` diff is empty\nThe C `.so` exports exactly 9 public symbols; the Rust `.so` exports the same 9, with matching symbol types:\n\n| symbol | type | |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cp_inflate`, `load_png_mem` | `T` | functions |\n| `cp_fixed_table`, `cp_permutation_order`, `cp_len_extra_bits`, `cp_len_base`, `cp_dist_extra_bits`, `cp_dist_base` | `D` | tables — **byte-identical contents and sizes** (verified by extracting the bytes from both ELF images) |\n| `cp_error_reason` | `B` | `.bss` pointer |\n\nThere are no macro-renamed symbols in this library (no namespace macros in `lib.h`).\n\n## Fidelity techniques\n`#[repr(C)] cp_state_t` reproduces the C layout exactly (`sizeof == 2464`, verified against `offsetof` in C) so the C's out-of-bounds `tree[lo-1]` read hits the same neighbouring struct field — that path fires ~33 k times in testing. All arithmetic uses wrapping ops matching x86 semantics, pointer arithmetic distinguishes C's sign-extended `ptr + int` (`cp_chunk`) from zero-extended `ptr + uint32_t` (`cp_find`), the unsigned `(int64_t)w*h*sizeof(...) < INT_MAX` check is reproduced, and `memcpy`/`memset` are the real libc ones. Bugs are preserved (`w = make32+1`, the inverted stored-block bound check, dead \"invalid image size found\" checks, the `innapropriate` typo).\n\n## Differential verification vs. the C `.so` (~16 900 comparisons)\nEach case ran in a forked child with zero-padded inputs and a deterministically-primed heap; every C result was produced twice so nondeterministic cases (the C reads uninitialized heap on truncated streams) are excluded rather than mistaken for logic diffs.\n\n| suite | cases | real mismatches |\n|---|---|---|\n| structured PNGs (all 5 colour types, filters 0-4, levels 0/1/6/9, split IDATs, palettes/tRNS, malformed) + inflate | 3 070 | 4 |\n| targeted paths (bad filter bytes, stored blocks, hand-built fixed-Huffman streams, huge chunk lengths, block type 3) | 599 | 0 |\n| fuzz (3 120 mutated PNGs + 2 500 mutated deflate streams × 4 input alignments) | 13 120 | 5 |\n| API/ABI edge driver (negative/zero sizes, NULL, unaligned pointers, repeated calls, mutation of the writable exported tables) | 94 | 0 |\n| C program linked directly against `lib.h` (struct-by-value return, tables, `cp_inflate`) | 3 images | 0 |\n\nPath coverage was measured with an instrumented C build: all 5 filter cases in both the first-row and later-row code, all 4 `cp_convert` widths, depalette with/without tRNS, stored/fixed/dynamic blocks, symbols 16/17/18, the distance-1 `memset` path, and 26/26 error strings.\n\n## The 9 remaining mismatches\nAll are the *same* input class: `cp_dynamic` writes up to ~50 bytes past its 320-byte stack array `lens[288+32]` (confirmed by instrumentation: writes to `lens[320..369]`), smashing the C stack frame — the C reference dies with SIGSEGV/SIGABRT. That is undefined behaviour whose outcome depends on the compiler's frame layout (the same input segfaults in the CMake `-O3` build, aborts under stack-protector, and completes normally in an `-O2` build). Rust reserves slack instead of corrupting its frame and returns the error the C would have reported. Where the C does *not* crash, the Rust matches bit-for-bit, including cases that overflow that array harmlessly.\n\nTwo notes: `assert()` is treated as a no-op (NDEBUG semantics) — with an assert-enabled C build, malformed *raw `cp_inflate`* streams abort; zero of 1 790 PNG inputs did. And behaviour that depends on uninitialized `malloc` memory (truncated deflate streams leave filter bytes unwritten) is not reproducible by anything — the C reference gives different answers run-to-run there, which I demonstrated explicitly. `c_src/` is unmodified (original timestamps and checksums intact).","ttft_ms":2111,"ttft_stream_ms":1696,"time_to_request_ms":34,"type":"result","duration_ms":3954767,"uuid":"cad8ab4a-ccc2-4d8a-a7a0-4b0b948214ef"}
